<title>USA: Cummins to build new engine in Indiana.</title>
<headline>Cummins to build new engine in Indiana.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ind. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cummins Engine Co Inc said Tuesday it planned to begin producing a new heavy-duty truck engine next March at a facility here.</p>
<p>The plant is undergoing a $225 million expansion, Cummins said. The new engine has an electronic dual overhead cam and 600 horsepower with improved torque.</p>
<p>Cummins said it believed the engine would help it capture a larger share of the heavy-duty truck market and improve its profitability.</p>
<p>	    -- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
